    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Annotations
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->

    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#ACTOR_TO_ROLE_RELATION">
        <rdfs:comment>Relationship that captures how an Actor takes on - or plays - a Business Role in order to perform a Physical Business Process</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#APP_APP_TO_BUS_RELATION">
        <rdfs:comment>An Application supports a Business Process, Activty or Task, optionally requiring an Application Service Qualities.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#APP_PRO_TO_PHYS_BUS_RELATION">
        <rdfs:comment>Defines the relationship between a specific Application Provider OR Application Provider Role and a specific physical process</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#APP_SVC_TO_BUS_RELATION">
        <rdfs:comment>An Application Service supports a Business Process, Activity or Task, optionally requiring an Application Service Qualities.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Actor">
        <rdfs:comment>A specific, named, group, team or individual that performs a role in a prcess.
Actors are used to capture how the enterprise is actually organized, in terms of the real companies, divisions, teams and individuals that make up the organization.
Actos take on the Roles (defined in the organization design) to execute Physical processes/activities.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Architecture_Objective">
        <rdfs:comment>A strategic goal associated with the Application Architecture of the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Architecture_Principle">
        <rdfs:comment>High level rules that govern the manner in which application capabilityes are implemented by the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Capability">
        <rdfs:comment>Provides the abstract perspective on the functional behaviour required to support the business.
Capabilities are mapped to the Business Domain that they support.
One of the additional purposes of this meta class is to provide a grounding for Applications Functions, enabling one to model that a particular Application Function &quot;is a one of these Application Capabilities&quot;</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Driver">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to define and manage the internal and external influences that motivate the Application Objectives.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Family">
        <rdfs:comment>A convenience component for defining types of applications.
Enables the application modeller to specify that 2 Application Providers are each a type of an Application. 
e.g. applicaitonProviderX and applicationProviderY are types of SAP (Application).
In addition, this can be used to group Application Providers under a name by which they are commonly refrerred to in the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Function">
        <rdfs:comment>A discrete piece of functional behaviour that an application provides. e.g. GetAllExchangeRates, MakeCredoitCardPayment</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Function_Implementation">
        <rdfs:comment>An implementation of an Application Function provided by an application - whether bespoke or packaged. e.g a doCreditCardPayment transaction in SAP Finance implements a MakeCreditCardPayment Application Function.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Provider">
        <rdfs:comment>An Application Provider provides one or more Application Services.
To provide a service, the Application Provider should provide - through its Application Function Implementations - all of the Application Functions of the Application Service that this Application Provider provides.
e.g. a specific implementation of SAP R/3 - the ERP System, the Finance System, Cast Iron Expenses project.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Application_Service">
        <rdfs:comment>A well-defined component of functional behaviour that provides a logical grouping of related Application Functions, e.g. ExchangeRates Service, CreditCardPayment Service or logical application such as CRM System, ERP System.
The specification of the service - in terms of what it does - is defined by the set of Application Functions that it provides.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Capability">
        <rdfs:comment>Models the capabilities of a business or enterprise.
Capabilities belong to business domains and represent the services that a business offers or requires or Business Process &quot;areas&quot;</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Capability_Chain">
        <rdfs:comment>An architecture that defines the flow of high level Business Capabilities (e.g. Value Chain, Demand Chain)</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Capability_Chain_Type">
        <rdfs:comment>Super class of the usages that appear in Business Capability Chain Diagram (Business Capability Chain).
Also a convenience super class to support use of the Protege Graph Widget.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Domain">
        <rdfs:comment>Business Domain meta class from the Conceptual view of the Business Architecture.
This is the top level (and least specific) construct in the Business Architecture.
It provides a means of categorizing business related elements independent of the context in which it is applied.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Driver">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to manage business drivers (internal and external influences) which motivate the organization to its business objectives.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Objective">
        <rdfs:comment>A strategic business goal for an enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Principle">
        <rdfs:comment>High level rules that govern the manner in which business capabilities are delivered by the enterprise</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Process">
        <rdfs:comment>Business Processes implement the Business Capabilities, and consist of Business Activities.
Processes are performed by Business Roles.
Business Processes represent specifications or designs of how processes should be performed.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Process_Family">
        <rdfs:comment>Used to group business processes, activities or tasks that are variants of each other into a single &apos;family&apos;, allowing them to be distinct while at the same time ceonvetying that they are related.
This provides a more powerful and flexible approach than using Enumerations or Taxonomies as it allows contextual information to be added, for example, Business Process X is a standard for the EMEA region within its Business Process Family</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Process_Type">
        <rdfs:comment>Super class of Business Process, Business Activity and Business Task.
Can be used to generically refer to Business Process work constructs, e.g. Used for mapping relationships from Application constructs.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Role">
        <rdfs:comment>Used to represent the logical design of the organization in terms of the roles that are required.
Group Business Roles represent a collection of responsibilities that are taken on by organization.
Individual Business Roles are responsbilities that you would expect to be taken on by an individual or individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Business_Role_Type">
        <rdfs:comment>Business Role types are used to define a taxonomy for Business Roles</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Dynamic_Application_Provider_Architecture">
        <rdfs:comment>Architecture defining the dynamic behaviour of the implementation of a function implementation.
This architecture defines how the Application Providers that are used in the architecture interact (by requesting Function Implementation) in order to deliver the behaviour of the Function Impelmentation.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#External_Conceptual_Business_Event">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to represent Conceptual Events that are raised by parties external to the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Geographic_Location">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to manage specific point geographical locations.
Unlike the Geographical Region, locations have a geocode to identify that location, e.g. cities, towns, streets.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Information_Architecture_Objective">
        <rdfs:comment>A strategic goal associated with the Information Architecture of the enterprise</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Logical_Software_Architecture">
        <rdfs:comment>A high level logical software architecture model for an Application Provider, comprised of Software Component Usages, Information Representations and their relationships.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Physical_Activity">
        <rdfs:comment>An instance of a Business Activity that is performed by a group or individual in the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Physical_Process">
        <rdfs:comment>An instance of a Business Process that is performed by a gorup or individual in the enterprise.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Physical_Process_Type">
        <rdfs:comment>Base class for the Physical Business Process meta classes.
Holds basic information and the relation to Application Providers and Application Function Implementations that support this process.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Product">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to capture the products that are produced by the enterprise.
Products are instances of Product Types.
E.g. in the motor manufacturer example, products could be &quot;Focus&quot;, &quot;Mustang&quot; as instances of the &quot;Car&quot; type.
Equally, a service company would capture the service offerings.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Product_Concept">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to define conceptual level representations of Products.
Used to define fundamentally WAHT a typye of product is, e.g. a motor manufacturer, such as car, truck etc., whereas a service organization would define the classes of service that they provide.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Product_Type">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to capture types of products that are produced by the enterprise.
Product Types are realizations of Product Concepts, and group the actual, physical products by type.
E.g. in the motor manufacturer exampe, product types would by &quot;Car&quot;, &quot;Truck&quot; as realizations of the &quot;Vehicle&quot; concept.
As a further example, a service company would define the types of a particular service (e.g. financial services) that they provide.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#SCA-RELATION">
        <rdfs:comment>Relationships between elements of a Software Component Architecture</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Site">
        <rdfs:comment>A specific (and named) physical location where processes or activities take place.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Site_Category">
        <rdfs:comment>A type of site at which Business Roles operate, e.g. a factory, an office, a warehouse.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Skill_Type">
        <rdfs:comment>Conceptual class that is used to provide a taxonomy and semantic grounding for business skill instances.
Instances of Skill_Type should be readily understood without any specialist knowledge.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Static_Application_Provider_Architecture">
        <rdfs:comment>The architecture describing the sub components of an Application Providers - a STATIC view.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Static_Application_Service_Architecture">
        <rdfs:comment>The architecture describing the sub components of an Application Service - a STATIC view and static dependencies between them.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Technology_Architecture_Objective">
        <rdfs:comment>A strategic goal associated with the Technology Architecture of the enterprise</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Time_Based_Conceptual_Business_Event">
        <rdfs:comment>Class to represent Conceptual Events that are raised by schedules or are timed events.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Value_Stage">
        <rdfs:comment>An activity that, as part of a Value Stream, contributes to the delivery of an outcome for a customer.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/xiaoqi/ontologies/2026/2/eamm#Value_Stream">
        <rdfs:comment>An end to end collection of activities that delivers an outcome for a customer.</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing">
        <rdfs:label>EAMM</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    


